cade of of losses  among a lot of  a lot of banks um and really what it is  is basically you just got settlement  risk if you don't have  it's it's like you know trading a  baseball card right both  both people hold on to the baseball card  and then they let go at the same time  that's uh that's uh uh you know you're  again kids kids tend to have the uh the  better understanding  of the way the world should work right  and the adults screwed it up  and set up these um very different  settlement cycles  for uh for for for for dollars  um and then there are a lot of wrinkles  inside of it too  uh fed wires can be reversed most folks  don't know that  you don't have settlement finality with  fed wire and then ach is a very big deal  um because you ach transactions for  consumers  they can reverse an ach transaction for  60 days beyond the settlement beyond the  statement period  and if you're at the beginning of your  statement cycle that means  your ach transaction isn't actually  settled for 90 days so this is the  reason why the crypto companies  have uh you know if you put if you if  you ach  uh a dollar payment into one of the  crypto exchanges  they typically don't give you access to  it right away they they want to know if  you're going to try to take it back  um and there's a lot of ach fraud you  know we  i think most folks are aware of the  chargeback risk and credit cards but  there's chargeback risk in dollar  payments too  so those are a lot of the real world  problems and when we started working on  some of our products we  we spent a lot of time talking to  institutional traders  but also just users of of the payment  system you know keep in mind i came from  the corporate world  corporate treasury world um working with  corporate treasurers when i was on wall  street  and uh they live this pain every day  um there's a there are a lot of problems  with the fact that the us dollar  payments are delayed so  i i figured out pretty early on and and  i haven'